"Surah al-Ma'un criticizes a life that leaves religion merely in words and is devoid of mercy and responsibility. Here, Elmalılı emphasizes that religion must be understood together with morality, worship, and social sensitivity.\n\nPushing the orphan away and not encouraging the feeding of the poor is the sign of a heart that does not take accountability in the Hereafter seriously. The surah reminds us that faith must be visible in one's conduct toward the weak and vulnerable in society.\n\nThose who perform prayer yet are heedless of their prayer are also warned. The problem here is not prayer itself, but detaching prayer from its spirit and turning it into ostentation or mere habit.\n\n'Preventing ma'un' means withholding even seemingly small acts of assistance. According to Elmalılı, true religious devotion also encompasses everyday kindnesses and small gestures of support in times of need.\n\nIn short, the surah states that worship must be completed with mercy, sincerity, and assistance."